From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: never hold an accepted unlock open for a message

A password that had already been accepted could leave the lock screen
up with its spinner turning, until the prompt was cancelled and the
password typed again. PAM logged success and no exception was raised;
the session simply stayed locked.

ScreenShield.deactivate() does not unlock anything itself. It calls
UnlockDialog.finish(), which calls AuthPrompt.finish(), which waited --
with no bound -- for the verifier to emit no-more-messages. That queue is
advanced by the promise handed to the show-message signal, and for a
fingerprint error that promise is a wiggle animation. So a successful
authentication was made to depend on an animation completing, which is
also why the fault needed an idle screen to appear: fprintd cancels its
own ongoing verify when it idles, pam_fprintd reports the resulting
no-match as an error, and that error was at the head of the queue at the
moment the password was accepted. Cancelling and retrying worked because
the retry found the queue empty.

The wait is now bounded, and whatever was still queued is logged, so the
next occurrence names its cause instead of being inferred.

diff --git a/js/gdm/authPrompt.js b/js/gdm/authPrompt.js
--- a/js/gdm/authPrompt.js
+++ b/js/gdm/authPrompt.js
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 const TimerChildProxy = Gio.DBusProxy.makeProxyWrapper(TimerChildIface);
 
 const DEFAULT_BUTTON_WELL_ICON_SIZE = 16;
+
+//: How long a completed authentication will wait for the verifier's message
+//: queue before going ahead without it. Long enough for a fingerprint error to
+//: be read and its wiggle to run, short enough that nobody sees a stall.
+const FINISH_MESSAGE_QUEUE_TIMEOUT = 2000;
 const DEFAULT_BUTTON_WELL_ANIMATION_DELAY = 1000;
 
 // A widget displayed instead of the unlock prompt
@@ -833,11 +838,43 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        const signalId = this._userVerifier.connect('no-more-messages', () => {
-            this._userVerifier.disconnect(signalId);
+        // This gates ScreenShield.deactivate(): until onComplete runs, a
+        // password that has already been accepted leaves the lock screen up
+        // with its spinner turning. Waiting for the queue without a bound made
+        // a successful unlock depend on an animation finishing -- the queue is
+        // advanced by the promise handed to show-message, and for a fingerprint
+        // error that promise is a wiggle. After the screen had blanked and
+        // fprintd cancelled its own verify, that error sat at the head of the
+        // queue and the session stayed locked until the prompt was cancelled
+        // and the password typed a second time.
+        //
+        // An accepted authentication is not allowed to hang on a message, so
+        // the wait is bounded and what was still queued is recorded, which
+        // names the cause rather than leaving it to be inferred.
+        let done = false;
+        let signalId = 0;
+        let timeoutId = 0;
+        const complete = () => {
+            if (done)
+                return;
+            done = true;
+            if (timeoutId)
+                GLib.source_remove(timeoutId);
+            if (signalId)
+                this._userVerifier.disconnect(signalId);
             this._userVerifier.clear();
             onComplete();
-        });
+        };
+
+        signalId = this._userVerifier.connect('no-more-messages', complete);
+        timeoutId = GLib.timeout_add_once(GLib.PRIORITY_DEFAULT,
+            FINISH_MESSAGE_QUEUE_TIMEOUT, () => {
+                timeoutId = 0;
+                const stuck = this._userVerifier.currentMessage;
+                log('gdm: completing the unlock without the message queue; ' +
+                    `still queued: ${stuck ? `${stuck.serviceName} type ${stuck.type}` : 'nothing'}`);
+                complete();
+            });
     }
 
     cancel() {
